===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# An effortful attempt to escape something dangerous, usually out of fear for one's life or health.
#* {{quote-web|en|date=2026-09-03|work=Skip Boring|author=Shreya Lele|title=The “Lady of the Dunes” Was Found Murdered in 1974. Nearly 50 Years Later, She Got Her Name Back|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20260903233651/https://skipboring.com/lady-of-the-dunes-ruth-marie-terry/|text=The most striking detail was the absence of any sign of '''struggle'''. It looked as though the woman had made no attempt to fight back, evident from the lack of bruises/wounds on her body. It was probable that she had not expected the attack.}}
# {{lb|en|figurative}} [[strife|Strife]], [[contention]], great [[effort]].
#* {{RQ:Maxwell Mirror and the Lamp|chapter=23|passage=The '''struggle''' with ways and means had recommenced, more difficult now a hundredfold than it had been before, because of their increasing needs. Their income disappeared as a little rivulet that is swallowed by the thirsty ground. He worked night and day to supplement it.}}
#* {{quote-journal
|en
|url=https://www.tikkun.org/book-review-textual-activism-by-rabbi-mike-moskowitz
|year=2019
|author=Rachel Timoner
|journal=Tikkun
|title=Book Review: Textual Activism by Rabbi Mike Moskowitz
|text=R. Moskowitz charges cisgender readers to be as conscious and deliberate with our religious identities as transgender and gender non-conforming people are with theirs, arguing that holiness is only achieved through continuous and unrelenting '''struggle''' and change.|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20260302032920/https://www.tikkun.org/book-review-textual-activism-by-rabbi-mike-moskowitz/|archivedate=2 March 2026}}

