===Verb===
{{en-verb}}

# {{lb|en|intransitive}} To [[strive]], to [[labour]] in [[difficulty]], to [[fight]] (''for'' or ''against''), to [[contend]].
#: {{syn|en|agonize|q1=literary}}
#: {{ux|en|During the centuries, the people of Ireland '''struggled''' constantly to assert their right to govern themselves.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|year=1951|month=October|title=Notes and News: The Harmonium at Troutbeck|journal=Railway Magazine|page=709|text=[[Troutbeck]] is a tiny village midway between Penrith and Keswick in a very sparsely populated part of Cumberland, and it used to be said by facetious travellers that the reason why it ever had a station at all was to give the engine a rest after it had '''struggled''' up the long and trying incline from Threlkeld.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|date=October 1, 2011|author=Tom Fordyce|work=BBC Sport
|title=[http://news.bbc.co.uk/sport2/hi/rugby_union/15124512.stm Rugby World Cup 2011: England 16-12 Scotland]
|passage=England were ponderous with ball in hand, their runners static when taking the ball and their lines obvious, while their front row '''struggled''' badly in the scrum.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|date=2013-06-28|author=w:Joris Luyendijk
|volume=189|issue=3|page=21|magazine=w:The Guardian Weekly
|title=[http://www.guardian.co.uk/commentisfree/joris-luyendijk-banking-blog/2013/jun/19/banking-britain-beyond-control Our banks are out of control]
|passage=Seeing the British establishment '''struggle''' with the financial sector is like watching an alcoholic who still resists the idea that something drastic needs to happen for him to turn his life around.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|date=2022-01-12|author=Paul Clifton|title=Network News: Emergency timetables as absences surge due to COVID|journal=RAIL|issue=948|page=6|text=Most train operators have reduced services with emergency timetables, as they '''struggle''' to cope with a rapid increase in staff absences due to the Omicron variant of COVID.}}
#* {{RQ:en:CNN|author=Chelsea Bailey|title=‘Take his pulse, he’s blue’: Bodycam footage shows fatal encounter between epileptic Indiana man and first responders|url=https://www.cnn.com/2024/09/30/us/rhyker-earl-bodycam-footage-epilepsy/index.html|date=2024-09-30|passage=The sheriff’s office released a compilation of bodycam footage Friday from deputies at the scene that shows them handcuffing Earl and pinning him down for more than 20 minutes as he '''struggles''' and repeatedly shouts for help.|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20251219121144/https://www.cnn.com/2024/09/30/us/rhyker-earl-bodycam-footage-epilepsy/index.html|archivedate=19 December 2025}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|date=2026 January 7|author='Mystery Shopper'|title=Cornish cream - without the jams?|journal=RAIL|issue=1052|page=48|text=At [[Par]], 150207 is the unit for the 1416 to [[Newquay]]. It is quite tatty and lacks tables - but does have plug sockets. It sounds laboured as it leaves, and while it sounds like it's '''struggling''' as it tackles [[Luxulyan]], it's not losing time.}}
# {{lb|en|intransitive}} To have [[difficulty]] with something.
#: {{ux|en|One of the doctor’s patients '''struggled''' with depression.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1972|author1=w:Mortimer J. Adler|author2=w:Charles Van Doren|title=w:How to Read a Book|text=Then our first effort must be to identify the actual words. Only after recognizing them individually can we begin to try to understand them, to '''struggle''' with perceiving what they mean.|isbn=0-671-21209-5|lccn=72-81451|page=17|pageurl=https://books.google.co.in/books?id=Z5PpkQadm5EC&pg=PA17&source=gbs_toc_r&cad=2#v=onepage&q&f=false}}
# {{lb|en|intransitive}} To strive, or to make efforts, with a twisting, or with contortions of the body.
#: {{ux|en|She '''struggled''' to escape from her assailant's grasp.}}
#* {{RQ:Jefferies Amateur Poacher|chapter=II|passage=Orion hit a rabbit once; but though sore wounded it got to the bury, and, '''struggling''' in, the arrow caught the side of the hole and was drawn out. Indeed, a nail filed sharp is not of much avail as an arrowhead; you must have it barbed, and that was a little beyond our skill.}}

